      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.099,
            0.443,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "**(c) decomposition reaction.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.121,
            0.433,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": "**(d) displacement reaction.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.141,
            0.894,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "**3. What happens when dilute hydrochloric acid is added to iron fillings? Tick the correct answer.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.179,
            0.639,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Hydrogen gas and iron chloride are produced.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.2,
            0.643,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Chlorine gas and iron hydroxide are produced.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.222,
            0.442,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "**(c) No reaction takes place.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.242,
            0.526,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Iron salt and water are produced.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.263,
            0.894,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "**4. What is a balanced chemical equation? Why should chemical equations be balanced?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.3,
            0.892,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "**5. Translate the following statements into chemical equations and then balance them.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.322,
            0.726,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Hydrogen gas combines with nitrogen to form ammonia.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.343,
            0.84,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Hydrogen sulphide gas burns in air to give water and sulpur dioxide.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.364,
            0.894,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Barium chloride reacts with aluminium sulphate to give aluminium chloride and a precipitate of barium sulphate.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.401,
            0.894,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Potassium metal reacts with water to give potassium hydroxide and hydrogen gas.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.439,
            0.551,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": "**6. Balance the following chemical equations.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.46,
            0.531,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": "**(a)** $\\mathrm{HNO_{3}+Ca(OH)_{2}\\rightarrow Ca(NO_{3})_{2}+H_{2}O}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.482,
            0.509,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": "**(b)** $\\mathrm{NaOH}+\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{SO}_{4}\\rightarrow\\mathrm{Na}_{2}\\mathrm{SO}_{4}+\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.502,
            0.504,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "**(c)** $\\mathrm{NaCl+AgNO_{3}\\rightarrow AgCl+NaNO_{3}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.523,
            0.499,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "**(d)** $\\mathrm{BaCl_{2}+H_{2}SO_{4}\\rightarrow BaSO_{4}+HCl}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.544,
            0.756,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "**7. Write the balanced chemical equations for the following reactions.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.565,
            0.832,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Calcium hydroxide + Carbon dioxide → Calcium carbonate + Water**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.585,
            0.616,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Zinc + Silver nitrate → Zinc nitrate + Silver**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.606,
            0.796,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Aluminium + Copper chloride → Aluminium chloride + Copper**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.628,
            0.894,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Barium chloride + Potassium sulphate → Barium sulphate + Potassium chloride**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.648,
            0.894,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "**8. Write the balanced chemical equation for the following and identify the type of reaction in each case.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.686,
            0.846,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Potassium bromide(aq) + Barium iodide(aq) → Potassium iodide(aq) +**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.639,
            0.708,
            0.814,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "**Barium bromide(s)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.728,
            0.704,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Zinc carbonate(s) → Zinc oxide(s) + Carbon dioxide(g)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.749,
            0.681,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Hydrogen(g) + Chlorine(g) → Hydrogen chloride(g)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.77,
            0.893,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Magnesium(s) + Hydrochloric acid(aq) → Magnesium chloride(aq) + Hydrogen(g)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.791,
            0.881,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "**9. What does one mean by exothermic and endothermic reactions? Give examples.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.812,
            0.739,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "**10. Why is respiration considered an exothermic reaction? Explain.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.833,
            0.894,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "**11. Why are decomposition reactions called the opposite of combination reactions? Write equations for these reactions.**"
        },
        {
